<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kauthara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kauthara was one of the principal regions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a>, around modern Nha Trang in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. Its chief sanctuary was the Po Nagar temple, dedicated to the goddess Yan Po Nagar, whose inscriptions go back to the 8th century. The region was lost to the Vietnamese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nguyen-lords">Nguyễn lords</a> in 1653.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kauthara.jpg" alt="Kauthara" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: wileypics · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PonNagarChamTowers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
